{"uncertainty": 0.12, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root-cause analysis: debounce lets short low glitches through", "summary": "Conclusion: rtl_bug. The approved RTL [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] states its own intent in its header: 'A change on `noisy`, in either direction, restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches `clean`.' The logic does not do this. It restarts the counter only on a rising change (`if (noisy && !prev) cnt <= 4'd0;`). On a falling change it keeps counting, or stays saturated at STABLE-1. The output gate is `noisy == prev && cnt == STABLE-1`.\n\nMechanism, with STABLE=4: after a long high, cnt has saturated at 3 and clean is 1. Noisy then drops for 2 edges. At edge A, noisy differs from prev, so clean holds, and cnt is not cleared. At edge B, noisy equals prev at 0 and cnt is 3, so clean takes 0. A 2-edge low glitch therefore reaches clean. High glitches are filtered correctly, which is why the defect is direction-specific.\n\nThis matches the triage evidence. [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1] / [run:run-0001] give 'Likely RTL bug' as the top hypothesis, although that classification has low confidence. [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] / [run:run-0002] show the failure reproducing deterministically: 1 of 1 checks failed and $finish was reached at time 175000.\n\nRanked hypotheses and the evidence that would refute each:\n(1) rtl_bug, missing restart on the falling change. Refuted if a low pulse of 4 edges or fewer, applied after clean has settled high, leaves clean at 1 on this RTL. The new repro testbench is the check for this.\n(2) testbench_bug, a wrong expectation in the upstream repro. Rejected: the expectation follows the RTL's own header contract. The new testbench also checks the high-glitch and settle behaviour, which are expected to pass, so a failure isolates the low-glitch path.\n(3) infrastructure, a simulator or flow artefact. Rejected: [run:run-0002] built the design, reached $finish and reported a check verdict, which points to a deterministic functional mismatch rather than a tool fault. It would be refuted only if the same sources produced different verdicts across runs.\n(4) spec_ambiguity. Rejected: the header says 'in either direction' and 'high or low' explicitly. It would be refuted only if an external specification that overrides the header allowed asymmetric filtering; none is among the inputs.\n\nSuggested fix, for the design owner to make: restart on any change, i.e. `if (noisy != prev) cnt <= 4'd0;`.\n\nThis traces to [requirement:req-19189b08df]."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/debounce_rca_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: low glitch passes through debounce", "summary": "This is a self-checking testbench for the RTL in [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], STABLE=4. It makes three counted checks:\n(1) a 2-edge high pulse from the reset-low state must not reach clean;\n(2) a long high must settle clean to 1;\n(3) after settling high, a 2-edge low pulse must never drive clean to 0.\nOn the RTL under investigation, check 3 is expected to fail, following the falling-edge restart defect behind [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2]. The testbench prints the single NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the run nonce just before $finish. It serves [requirement:req-19189b08df].", "entry": "debounce_rca_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["Running tb/debounce_rca_tb.v against debounce_rise_only_restart.v is expected to report 2 passed, 1 failed; this has not been run by me.", "Changing the restart condition to `noisy != prev` is expected to make all three checks pass; not executed.", "No separate specification document was read; the RTL header comment is treated as the design contract."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Independent review (review_record) is still required for this task, and the simulator.run repro gate must be met first. I have not approved or verified anything myself. The existing review record [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.e1] covers the RTL fixture, not this analysis."}
